  "report": "# S001 invalidation: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation check: 16 of 16 killed\n\nLimitations: recompute is a harness-supplied derivation evaluated for the keys SemDB marks affected; the crate has no query engine, so nothing is claimed about a real derivation or its cost; prepare_delta clones the whole state and affected_by rebuilds the reverse map per call (O(edges)): the invalidation step is not O(affected); only the recomputation has locality, and wall-clock time grows with the graph whatever the blast radius; with a correct host the affected set equals the structural closure, so the locality ratio on the local-change class is bounded by the class (50 per mille) and the 250 threshold only catches a host that over-invalidates by more than a factor of five; exactness is closure_mismatches; SemDB has no early cutoff: precision against the value-changed set (precision_value_permille, the number of unnecessary_invalidations beyond the coverage floor of one) is descriptive and low on lossy derivations by design; synthetic seeded DAGs of up to 4096 keys with small integer values, one process, one machine profile; deltas above MAX_DELTA_ITEMS, the ConflictingOperation refusal, removal with dangling dependents, StalePreparation and the journal encoding are not exercised; prepare_delta computes the closure over the old and over the new graph, and the two calls are redundant with each other: dropping either is an equivalent mutant and neither is in the mutation plan; 'over the old and the new edges' is the oracle's definition, not a tested distinction; the hub class is an ungated control; the negative controls doctor the set after the host produced it (they show the criteria can fail; the mutation evidence shows a defective host is caught); arm G is the harness derivation over the oracle's graph held equal to the oracle's own pass, not a third independent opinion; wall-clock times (timing_ns) are recorded and never judged.\n"
